From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sheepsticked <72666364+Sheepsticked@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] call start: ask AT+CLCC again; ATA and ATD wait 20 s

Upstream: https://github.com/IchthysMaranatha/asterisk-chan-quectel @ 3d45c7f072131296a7e3c1a4faf5bb18751dbd87
Purpose: one AT command answered late or not at all restarted the modem and
         ended every call on it, so a lost or slow answer at the start of a
         call (the modem busy with the network, or a USB transfer error)
         cost the call (applies on top of 0013)

An AT+CLCC that gets no answer within its 5 s is written once more and
waited for another 15 s. When both writes are answered, the first answer
only starts a 1 s wait for the second, so that a late answer is not taken
for the next command's. ATA and ATD wait 20 s instead of 5 s.
